nra|n|The oval or roundish body laid by domestic poultry and other birds, tortoises, etc. It consists of a yolk, usually surrounded by the "white" or albumen, and inclosed in a shell or strong membrane. ; A simple cell, from the development of which the young of animals are formed; ovum; germ cell. ; Anything resembling an egg in form.	N:1n4o,42,2~1n4o,42,2
nrv|n|The conscious and permanent subject of all psychical experiences, whether held to be directly known or the product of reflective thought; -- opposed to non-ego.	a:7sf,60,3~7sf,60,3
nsh|a|Surpassing; extraordinary; distinguished (in a bad sense); -- formerly used with words importing a good quality, but now joined with words having a bad sense; as, an egregious rascal; an egregious ass; an egregious mistake.	j:pwa,69,5;b9g,54,2~pwa,69,5;b9g,54,2	e:1hyf,71,3;1psw,45,4;1c22,40,8~1c22,40,8;1psw,45,4;1hyf,71,3
